# f3 = the constructor of Plain, f4 = the constructor of Noted
# A class has one `super(..)`, so the constructor that it names is copied into the constructor of the class below, once a class, as the body of a constructor function is copied where it is constructed.
# In the copy new.target is the class below: the object is made as a Noted, below the prototype of Noted, and nobody has to ask what the call has given.
# RUN(COPY): walk f4 mechanisms=all
